    "https://ap.washington.edu/ahr/position-details/?job_id=185209": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Position Details - Academic Personnel & Faculty Skip to content All the UW Current site Search scope All the UW Current site Enter search text University of Washington University of Washington UW HR Workday Employee Help UW Finance Faculty Senate Menu Home About us About Us Our Strategic Plan Leadership Team Office and Team Contacts Faculty Affairs Advisory Committee News News eDigest Archive For Academic Personnel For Academic Personnel & Faculty New Faculty @UW Faculty Development Faculty Inclusive Excellence ADVANCE Center for Institutional Change Faculty Review Resources Faculty Promotion & Tenure Librarian Reappointment & Promotion Academic Responsibilities Voting Guidelines Time Off and Leaves Postdoctoral Scholars Affairs & Operations Academic Personnel & Faculty Affairs Academic Titles and Ranks Resources Forms and Templates Policies and Procedures Appointment Actions Visas Academic Jobs Academic Personnel & Faculty Academic Personnel & Faculty Academic Personnel & Faculty Affairs Position Details Position Details Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Practice, Department of Family Medicine; Core Residency - Northgate Position Overview School / Campus / College: School of Medicine Organization: Family Medicine Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Practice, Department of Family Medicine; Core Residency - Northgate Position Details Position Description The Department of Family Medicine at the University of Washington invites applications for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Practice. Professorial rank is dependent upon record of academic and teaching success in addition to clinical expertise . We seek applicants who demonstrate commitment to excellence in teaching and service in a diverse and inclusive academic community. The successful candidate will join our faculty on a twelve-month full-time basis for a term of three years beginning November 1, 2026 or soon thereafter . Faculty on the Clinical Practice track are expected to demonstrate excellence in clinical care, professionalism, and teaching. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in the broad spectrum of ambulatory clinical practice at UW Northgate clinic and provide inpatient obstetrical care at UWMC Northwest Hospital. Postive factors for consideration include, but are not limited to, candidates with recent direct practivce - based patient care experience in full spectrum family medicine. The clinical full time equivalent ( cFTE ) will be 0.70 with an administrative component of 0.30. Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Practice are eligible for multiyear appointments that align with a 12-month service period (July 1–June 30). Faculty on a 12-month service period are paid for 11 months of service over 12 months, allowing the equivalent of one month of paid time off. The base salary range for Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice will be: $17,0 00 -$ 19,416 per month ($204 ,000-$2 33 , 000 annually) commensurate with experience and qualification or mandated by the U.S. Department of Labor prevailing wage determination. The base salary range for Associate Professor of Clinical Practice will be: $1 8,333 -$ 21,666 per month ($2 20,000 - $ 2 6 0 ,000 annually) commensurate with experience and qualification or mandated by the U.S. Department of Labor prevailing wage determination. Salary ranges are inclusive of base salary provided through the UW Physicians (UWP) practice plan, in addition to base salary provided by the University. Please note that only compensation provided by the University is included in university benefit determinations and calculations. Compensation provided by the UW Physicians (UWP) practice plan may provide eligibility for separate benefits offered by that organization. Other compensation associated with this position may include incentive through the UW Physicians practice plan and a stipend for call coverage. Reporting Structure All Department of Family Medicine faculty report to the Department Chair. This position will also have accountability to the Family Medicine Residency Program Director and the Northgate Medical Director. Position Responsibilities: This appointment is for a core faculty position in the Department of Family Medicine Residency Program. Duties include direct ambulatory patient care and precepting residents at the UW Medicine Northgate clinic. Duties also include inpatient Family Medicine OB attending resonsibilties at UWMC Northwest Hospital.  Core residency faculty provide direct teaching, advise learners and contribute to residency administration and curriculum. Core resident faculty members are expected to have a significant role in the education and supervision of residents and must, as a component of their activities, teach, evaluate, and provide formative feedback to residents. Qualifications Applicants for this clinical practice faculty position must meet the following minimum qualifications: Applicants are required to have an MD, DO, or foreign equivalent with current certification by the American Board of Family Medicine. License or license eligible in Washington State In order to be eligible for University sponsorship for an H-1B visa, graduate of foreign (non-U.S.) medical schools must show successful completion of all three steps of the U.S. Medical Licensing Exam (USMLE), or equivalent as determined by the Secretary of Health and Human Services. Instructions Applicants should include the following materials: A cover letter of no more than two pages detailing your interest in the position, relevant qualifications, and experiences A curriculum vitae Additional material- a vision statement – articulating how your past experiences and/or future plans in teaching, mentoring, patient care, and/or service promote a sense of belonging and foster a welcoming and inclusive environment. Please also include contact information for at least 2 referees who are prepared to provide letters of recommendation upon request . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Equal Opportunity The University of Washington is committed to fostering an inclusive, respectful and welcoming community for all. As an equal opportunity employer, the University considers applicants for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, citizenship, sex, pregnancy, age, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, disability, or veteran status consistent with UW Executive Order No. 81 . Benefits Information The University is committed to providing excellent benefits to our faculty. For a summary of available benefits, please see UWHR benefits information . Privacy Notice Your application materials may be used for employment consideration and shared in accordance with UW’s Privacy Policy. Disability Services The University of Washington is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Disability Services Office at 206-543-6450 or dso@uw.edu. Apply now The University of Washington is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. For help signing up, accessing your account, or submitting your application, please check out Interfolio's help and support section or get in touch via email at help@interfolio.com or phone at (877)997-8807. Title IX Notice The University of Washington does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits sex discrimination and sex-based harassment in its education programs and activities, including in admission and employment. Refer to the UW policies page on the Title IX website to review (1) the University’s policies prohibiting sex- and gender-based violence, harassment, and discrimination and (2) the related procedures for addressing complaints. Inquiries about Title IX may be referred to the University’s Title IX Coordinator , the U.S. Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights , or both. To report information or make a complaint about conduct that may constitute sex discrimination or sex-based harassment, submit an online Title IX report or email or call the Office of the Title IX Coordinator. Office of the Title IX Coordinator Valery Richardson, Title IX Coordinator 4311 11th Ave NE Seattle, WA 98105 206-221-7932 TitleIX@uw.edu ← Back to all positions University of Washington Be boundless Connect with us: Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Pinterest Accessibility Contact Us Jobs Campus Safety My UW Rules Docket Privacy Terms Newsletter © 2026 University of Washington  |  Seattle, WA"
    },
    "https://ap.washington.edu/ahr/position-details/?job_id=185212": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Position Details - Academic Personnel & Faculty Skip to content All the UW Current site Search scope All the UW Current site Enter search text University of Washington University of Washington UW HR Workday Employee Help UW Finance Faculty Senate Menu Home About us About Us Our Strategic Plan Leadership Team Office and Team Contacts Faculty Affairs Advisory Committee News News eDigest Archive For Academic Personnel For Academic Personnel & Faculty New Faculty @UW Faculty Development Faculty Inclusive Excellence ADVANCE Center for Institutional Change Faculty Review Resources Faculty Promotion & Tenure Librarian Reappointment & Promotion Academic Responsibilities Voting Guidelines Time Off and Leaves Postdoctoral Scholars Affairs & Operations Academic Personnel & Faculty Affairs Academic Titles and Ranks Resources Forms and Templates Policies and Procedures Appointment Actions Visas Academic Jobs Academic Personnel & Faculty Academic Personnel & Faculty Academic Personnel & Faculty Affairs Position Details Position Details Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Practice, Department of Family Medicine; Core Residency, Harborview Position Overview School / Campus / College: School of Medicine Organization: Family Medicine Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Practice, Department of Family Medicine; Core Residency, Harborview Position Details Position Description The Department of Family Medicine at the University of Washington invites applications for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Practice. Professorial rank is dependent upon record of academic and teaching success in addition to clinical expertise. We seek applicants who demonstrate commitment to excellence in teaching and service in a diverse and inclusive academic community. The successful candidate will join our faculty on a twelve-month full-time basis for a term of three years beginning October 1, 2026 or soon thereafter. Faculty on the Clinical Practice track are expected to demonstrate excellence in clinical care, professionalism, and teaching. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in the broad spectrum of ambulatory clinical practice at UW Harborview clinic and provide inpatient obstetrical care at UWMC Northwest Hospital. Positive factors for consideration include, but are not limited to, candidates with recent direct practice- based patient care experience in full spectrum family medicine. The clinical full time equivalent (cFTE) will be 0.70 with an administrative component of 0.30. Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Practice are eligible for multiyear appointments that align with a 12-month service period (July 1–June 30). Faculty on a 12-month service period are paid for 11 months of service over 12 months, allowing the equivalent of one month of paid time off. The base salary range for Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice will be: $17,000-$19,416 per month ($204,000-$233,000) annually commensurate with experience and qualification or mandated by the U.S. Department of Labor prevailing wage determination. The base salary range for Associate Professor of Clinical Practice will be: $18,333-$21,666 per month ($220,000- $260,000 ) annually commensurate with experience and qualification or mandated by the U.S. Department of Labor prevailing wage determination. Other compensation associated with this position may include incentive through the UW Physicians practice plan and stipends for call-coverage. Salary ranges are inclusive of base salary provided through the UW Physicians (UWP) practice plan, in addition to base salary provided by the University. Please note that only compensation provided by the University is included in university benefit determinations and calculations. Compensation provided by the UW Physicians (UWP) practice plan may provide eligibility for separate benefits offered by that organization. Reporting Structure All Department of Family Medicine faculty report to the Department Chair. This position will also have accountability to the Residency Program Director and the Harborview Family Medicine Clinic Medical Director. Position Responsibilities: This appointment is for a core faculty position in the Department of Family Medicine Residency Program based at the UW Family Medicine Harborview Clinic.  Duties include full-spectrum direct  patient care and resident precepting.  Duties also include attending responsibilites for the Family Medicine OB Servce based at UWMC Northwest Hospital.  Core residency faculty also provide direct teaching, advise learners and contribute to residency administration and curriculum. Core resident faculty members are expected to have a significant role in the education and supervision of residents and must, as a component of their activities, teach, evaluate, and provide formative feedback to residents. Qualifications Applicants for this clinical practice faculty position must meet the following minimum qualifications: Applicants are required to have an MD, DO, or foreign equivalent with current certification by the American Board of Family Medicine. License or license eligible in Washington State In order to be eligible for University sponsorship for an H-1B visa, graduate of foreign (non-U.S.) medical schools must show successful completion of all three steps of the U.S. Medical Licensing Exam (USMLE), or equivalent as determined by the Secretary of Health and Human Services. Instructions Applicants should include the following materials: A cover letter of no more than two pages detailing your interest in the position, relevant qualifications, and experiences A curriculum vitae Additional material- a vision statement – articulating how your past experiences and/or future plans in research, teaching, mentoring, patient care, and/or service promote a sense of belonging and foster a welcoming and inclusive environment. Please also include contact information for at least 2 referees who are prepared to provide letters of recommendation upon request . Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Equal Opportunity The University of Washington is committed to fostering an inclusive, respectful and welcoming community for all. As an equal opportunity employer, the University considers applicants for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, citizenship, sex, pregnancy, age, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, disability, or veteran status consistent with UW Executive Order No. 81 . Benefits Information The University is committed to providing excellent benefits to our faculty. For a summary of available benefits, please see UWHR benefits information . Privacy Notice Your application materials may be used for employment consideration and shared in accordance with UW’s Privacy Policy. Disability Services The University of Washington is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact the Disability Services Office at 206-543-6450 or dso@uw.edu. Apply now The University of Washington is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. For help signing up, accessing your account, or submitting your application, please check out Interfolio's help and support section or get in touch via email at help@interfolio.com or phone at (877)997-8807. Title IX Notice The University of Washington does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits sex discrimination and sex-based harassment in its education programs and activities, including in admission and employment. Refer to the UW policies page on the Title IX website to review (1) the University’s policies prohibiting sex- and gender-based violence, harassment, and discrimination and (2) the related procedures for addressing complaints. Inquiries about Title IX may be referred to the University’s Title IX Coordinator , the U.S. Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights , or both. To report information or make a complaint about conduct that may constitute sex discrimination or sex-based harassment, submit an online Title IX report or email or call the Office of the Title IX Coordinator. Office of the Title IX Coordinator Valery Richardson, Title IX Coordinator 4311 11th Ave NE Seattle, WA 98105 206-221-7932 TitleIX@uw.edu ← Back to all positions University of Washington Be boundless Connect with us: Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Pinterest Accessibility Contact Us Jobs Campus Safety My UW Rules Docket Privacy Terms Newsletter © 2026 University of Washington  |  Seattle, WA"
